#549 fbctrlportkill -- PRE-TABLE ADDENDUM for kill table 4, written BEFORE table 4 runs (this file's mtime is the order
proof; table4/ does not exist yet).

WHY A TABLE 4.  The closing pass on the 73-row repair (panel_20260925_141420, the dedicated grok job, and the Opus 5.5
seat which MEASURED ten 73/73 escapes, opus5_close.md) found edits conditioned on axis values the rows held only in
part: the previous selector (rows held 0, 5, 6, 7), the COMMAND cell (never non-zero at a refusal or a PORT read), the
read width (lw and ld only), the first refusal's width and predecessor, re-arms by a DATA read or a GET_RESOLUTION,
a value-conditional clobber on 8, the padding stores' 16 unobserved, and the announced value checked only when it is
narrow.  Three consecutive passes found such edits (pass 2: width; F2: width; closing: selector, COMMAND, read width),
so the repair is the CLASS CLOSURE: one diff that holds EVERY value of EVERY single axis for each effect, written into
the contract as an enumeration (the probe's header), with joint (two-axis) cells disclosed as clause (e).

THE DETECTOR CHANGE (L1, pre-ship).  73 rows -> 94; 8 sessions -> 13.  P: the two padding refusals (16 by sb, 16 by
sh) are now read back.  R: a DATA READ and a GET_RESOLUTION join the traffic between its refusals.  V: a PORT read right
after its first refusal (COMMAND holding 2, selector 1), a count after that first refusal and after the last, and 8 as
a fifth later refusal.  W: a count after its first refusal (8 by sb) and after its last, and lb/lh of PORT.  X2 X3 X4
X6 X7: fresh devices whose FIRST refusal is 9 by sh after 2, 0x100000003 by sd after 3 (whose announce must name that
value), 9 by sw after 4, 9 by sb after 6, 0x100 by sh after 7 -- count 1 and PORT keeps k.  The gate adds a
row-names-unique check (a row replaced by a copy of another kept every count; the closing grok seat).
Measured on the fix before this table: 94/94, CONTROL=OK, 8 s, 94 rows printed, no duplicate names.

DIFF OF THE PRESCRIBED ROWS (PRETABLE.out, _t2, _t3) AGAINST THE NEW PROBE: all 73 present.  RENAMED, same channel:
"R announce still 1 after DATA and NOP traffic" -> "... after DATA, NOP and GET_RESOLUTION"; "R refuse 9 after the NOP,
PORT keeps 5" -> "R refuse 9 after that traffic, PORT keeps 5"; V's "after four refusals" -> "after five refusals"
(eight rows).  Nothing prescribed was dropped.

PREDICTIONS FOR ALL 101 (mutants549_t4.py = table 3's 62 + 39 from the closing pass):
  PREDICTED 94/94, each DISCLOSED in the contract (14): M_static, M_noguard, T_D9c_serial1, N_acc32 (the fix's own
    binary), N_order, N_rdmask7, N_datard16, N_datawr8 -- table 3's eight -- and B_mod12 (a period of twelve),
    G5a_noexit and G5b_checkop (edits of the kept DATA check: unreachable), G7_ldbit32 and A2_sb3 (joint cells),
    A1_not10 (one value no row writes).
  PREDICTED RED (87), the closing escapes with the row predicted to catch each:
    E_rd_w4 C_rd_w4only   W's lb / lh rows              E_rd_cmd              V "refuse 9 while COMMAND holds 2"
    E_ref_p1 G1_rewrite1  V "PORT keeps 1"              E_ref_p2/p3/p4        X2 / X3 / X4 "PORT keeps k"
    E_ref_cmd             V "PORT keeps 1"              C_ref_p0 / C_ref_p7   F / P (as table 3's controls)
    E_ann_w4              W's first-refusal count, X2 X3 X6 X7 counts
    E_ann_p1 E_ann_cmd E_cmdset R_partAB                V "that first refusal announces"
    C_ann_nw4 C_ann_p5 S_ann_cp                         P / F announce rows (as measured by the Opus seat)
    B_mod11               P's twelve-refusal count      L1_rebit63            W's five-refusal count
    G2_rdrearm G3a_cmdrearm G3b_getresrearm             R's count after its traffic
    G4_pad16              P "refuse 16 (sb)" and "(sh)" G6_trunc32            X3 "names the wide value"
    G8_clob8              V "port 0 (COMMAND) still 2"  S_rd_idata S_ref_wp R_state1   as the Opus seat measured
    T_W_sd7               A "accept selector 7 written by sd"   T_W_sw8   P "refuse 8 (sw)"   T_W_sb0   W "accept 0 by sb"
  and every one of table 3's 54 reds, red again.
FLOOR: (a) HEAD fails (M_revert); (b) M_revert is HEAD's PORT arm verbatim; (c) the gate pins 94, reconciles the
printed rows with the trailer and requires unique row names; (d) every one-axis weakening or qualification of the three
dominating predicates, over every axis value, has a row -- the enumeration; (e) the contract, with joint cells named.
